    "narrative": "For today\u2019s slate, **Jos\u00e9 Ram\u00edrez** (77.25) and **Bryson Stott** (72.63) emerge as our clear offensive anchors. **Jos\u00e9 Ram\u00edrez** is effectively matchup-proof, even against a high-pedigree arm like Rod\u00f3n, and his high placement in the order combined with strong base metrics makes him our highest-ceiling asset. Similarly, **Bryson Stott** benefits significantly from a favorable platoon advantage against the struggling Scherzer; the 19% boost from the opposing SP\u2019s high xERA and his right-handed platoon edge solidify him as a priority start. **Lawrence Butler** is another high-value play at 67.98; despite being \"Lineup Pending,\" his projected spot against Sproat offers a superior mix of power and platoon leverage that keeps him comfortably in the active roster.\n\nWe are navigating a cluster of marginal plays as we face a difficult matchup against Griffin. Both **Luis Arraez** (47.17) and **Matt Chapman** (46.48) are suppressed by this opponent, and while **Jonathan Aranda** (49.05) and **Jung Hoo Lee** (42.39) round out the lineup, their scores reflect the difficulty of the individual matchups. **Gavin Sheets** (59.88) represents our best opportunity to capitalize on external conditions; despite a modest base projection, a favorable wind direction (+5%) and a manageable matchup against Singer keep his efficiency high enough to warrant a start. **Taylor Ward** (55.33) remains a viable option largely due to his leadoff role and park factors, which help offset the difficulty of facing Kirby.\n\nThe most difficult bench decision was choosing between **Masyn Winn** (45.59) and the lower-tier starters. **Masyn Winn** was the closest to cracking the lineup, but his efficiency was ultimately downgraded by a 41% rain risk and a negative park factor. Given the 1.87s pop time of the opposing catcher, we felt it was safer to bench **Masyn Winn** to prioritize the higher floor offered by our current UTIL and MI slots. While **Geraldo Perdomo** (45.57) was also considered, his raw projection failed to clear the threshold against the current options. We continue to monitor the status of **Cal Raleigh** and **Yainer Diaz**, both of whom remain sidelined on the IL, leaving our catching depth thin for the immediate future.",
